      "id": "grill",
      "title": "A goal, questioned",
      "plain": "A goal too big for one change is questioned one answer at a time, then written down as a spec and a plan of issues.",
      "technical": "planning grill, spec-write and plan-decompose leave the spec and its issues under .agents/plan/.",
      "focus": [
        "planning"
      ],
      "flows": [],
      "ms": 3000
    },
    {
      "id": "cards",
      "title": "One card, one session",
      "plain": "Each issue goes on the board as a card. A card you approve starts a session of its own, in its own worktree.",
      "technical": "agent-works orchestrate shows the plan's issues as cards; aw board grant records the yes, and dispatch starts card-<id> in a worktree.",
      "focus": [
        "planning",
        "agent-works"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "cards"
      ],
      "ms": 3200
    },
    {
      "id": "build",
      "title": "Test first, least code",
      "plain": "Each session writes a failing test first, then the least code that makes it pass.",
      "technical": "work-card follows delivery tdd: red, green, refactor. Its green step is code ladder, the first rung that holds.",
      "focus": [
        "agent-works",
        "delivery",
        "code"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "tdd",
        "ladder"
      ],
      "ms": 3200
    },
    {
      "id": "look",
      "title": "Judged by eye",
      "plain": "A card judged by eye is proved on a few shots, and waits its turn for the one renderer the sessions share.",
      "technical": "A card labelled look starts its child in perceptual-loop iterate-shots; the render runs under agent-works resource-locks.",
      "focus": [
        "agent-works",
        "perceptual-loop"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "look",
        "locks"
      ],
      "ms": 3200
    },
    {
      "id": "same-change",
      "title": "Docs in the same change",
      "plain": "The page, its screenshot and the map line go into the same change as the code, and the prose is in your voice.",
      "technical": "build-tdd calls docs-parity docs-sync, which writes prose through writing; system-map's Stop check asks for the @system line in this change.",
      "focus": [
        "docs-parity",
        "writing",
        "system-map"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "docs",
        "voice"
      ],
      "ms": 3400
    },
    {
      "id": "land",
      "title": "Reviewed, then landed",
      "plain": "The session opens a merge request. The orchestrator reads the diff, hunts what is not needed, and merges on green.",
      "technical": "The child ships with delivery ship; review-card runs code review, then delivery land merges the head it reviewed.",
      "focus": [
        "agent-works",
        "delivery",
        "code"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "review",
        "land"
      ],
      "ms": 3400
    },
